gamescope: run on a Vulkan device that names no DRM node (Venus over vtest)

On a Mali phone the runtime's Vulkan is Mesa's Venus over a vtest socket to a server on the
device's own driver. Venus reports VK_EXT_physical_device_drm with no primary and no render node,
has no VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd (vtest has no external sync), and can export dma-bufs (the
server's gralloc allocations) but never import one. With no node:

- createDevice runs as if the extension were absent instead of failing on the primary node;
- VK_KHR_external_semaphore_fd is optional and the Wayland backend offers no explicit sync
  (DRM syncobj timelines need a render node);
- flippable images skip the host's DRM_FORMAT_MOD_INVALID entry, and with no exportable modifier
  fall back to a plain LINEAR image exported as DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR (logged) instead of
  asserting;
- wl_shm uploads are not exported: they are copied again at every commit (the per-wlr_buffer memo
  kept showing the first copy of a redrawn wl_buffer), counted ready without a dma-buf fence,
  and composited - a layer with no host buffer forces composition, and a plane is only handed
  to the host when its texture has one.

A device with a DRM node (Turnip on Adreno) takes none of these paths: every new branch is keyed
on the device naming no node, or on a texture that has no backend fb, which only happens there.

